{"path":"thread/recursive_mutex/try_lock","title":"std::recursive_mutex::try_lock","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::recursive_mutex::</span>try_lock","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/recursive_mutex/try_lock","section":"thread","kind":"page","summary":"Tries to lock the mutex. Returns immediately. On successful lock acquisition returns true, otherwise returns false.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> try_lock<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Tries to lock the mutex. Returns immediately. On successful lock acquisition returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>, otherwise returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>.\n</p><p>This function is allowed to fail spuriously and return <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code> even if the mutex is not currently locked by any other thread.\n</p><p>A thread may call <code>try_lock</code> on a recursive mutex repeatedly. Successful calls to <code>try_lock</code> increment the ownership count: the mutex will only be released after the thread makes a matching number of calls to <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/recursive_mutex/unlock\">unlock</a></span>.  \n</p><p>The maximum number of levels of ownership is unspecified. A call to <code>try_lock</code> will return <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code> if this number is exceeded.\n</p><p>Prior <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/recursive_mutex/unlock\">unlock()</a></span> operation on the same mutex <i>synchronizes-with</i> (as defined in <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/atomic/memory_order\">std::memory_order</a></span>) this operation if it returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>. Note that prior <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/recursive_mutex/lock\">lock()</a></span> does not synchronize with this operation if it returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code> if the lock was acquired successfully, otherwise <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<p>Throws nothing.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;mutex&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/recursive_mutex\"><span class=\"kw2176\">std::<span class=\"me2\">recursive_mutex</span></span></a> test<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>test.<span class=\"me1\">try_lock</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"lock acquired<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        test.<span class=\"me1\">unlock</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">else</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"lock not acquired<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    test.<span class=\"me1\">lock</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// non-recursive mutex would return false from try_lock now</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>test.<span class=\"me1\">try_lock</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"lock acquired<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        test.<span class=\"me1\">unlock</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> \n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">else</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"lock not acquired<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    test.<span class=\"me1\">unlock</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>lock acquired\nlock acquired</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/recursive_mutex/lock\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>lock</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  locks the mutex, blocks if the mutex is not available <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/recursive_mutex/unlock\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>unlock</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  unlocks the mutex <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/thread/mtx_trylock\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>mtx_trylock</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"thread","title":"Concurrency support library (since C++11)"},{"path":"thread/recursive_mutex","title":"std::recursive_mutex"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::recursive_mutex::try_lock","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++11. Tries to lock the mutex. Returns immediately. On successful lock acquisition returns true, otherwise returns false."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"true if the lock was acquired successfully, otherwise false."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"Throws nothing."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"lock","note":"locks the mutex, blocks if the mutex is not available"},{"label":"unlock","note":"unlocks the mutex"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":231,"codeBlockCount":2}
